---
layout: base.njk
title: "Personas"
description: "The fabricated identities behind the LinkedIn accounts reported in connection with DPRK remote IT-worker operations, each gathering the indicators one report filed under that identity."
permalink: "/remote-workers/personas/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
extra_head: '<script src="/assets/js/persona-filter.js" defer></script>'
---
{#
  src/remote-workers/personas/index.njk — the persona listing

  One card per persona, each card a single link to its own page. The grouping
  and the reasoning behind it live in scripts/lib/personas.js, surfaced here
  through the `personas` global data file; cards come from
  partials/persona-card.njk.
#}
{% set active_tab = "personas" %}
{% set loosePhotos = iocs["x-dossiers"].unattributed_photos %}

<section>
  <h1>Personas</h1>
  {% include "partials/profiles-tab-bar.njk" %}
  <p>
    A DPRK IT-worker operation does not apply for work as a person; it applies
    as a persona — a fabricated professional identity with a name, a headshot,
    an employment history and the accounts to hold them. This page gathers the
    identifiers in the <a href="/remote-workers/">indicator index</a> into the
    persona each was reported under. The grouping is the reporting's own: two
    indicators appear together here only where one report, or one researcher,
    filed them under the same identity. A tile under a publisher's name rather
    than a person's is a photograph published with no address, account or name
    attached to it, and leads out to the page that published it.
  </p>
  {# Hidden in the markup and revealed by persona-filter.js, the same
     progressive-enhancement pattern as the /sources/ and /hunts/ filters.
     data-persona-limit caps the listing at that many cards until the reader
     asks for the rest; without JavaScript every card renders. The script
     rounds the cap up to the end of the row it falls in, so the last row
     before the button is a full one at every one of .profile-grid's column
     counts.
     Searching reaches into each persona's indicator list as well as its name,
     so an address or a handle finds the persona holding it — see the
     data-search attribute in partials/persona-card.njk. #}
  <div class="table-filter" data-persona-search data-persona-limit="{{ limits.list }}" hidden>
    {% set personaCountText %}{{ personas.length }} persona{% if personas.length != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% if loosePhotos.length %}, and {{ loosePhotos.length }} photograph{% if loosePhotos.length != 1 %}s{% endif %} published without an identifier{% endif %}. Select any one for the full record.{% endset %}{% set searchBox = { id: "persona-search-input", label: "Search personas", placeholder: "Name, alias, or an indicator such as an address or GitHub handle", attr: "data-persona-search-input", count: "data-persona-count", countText: personaCountText } %}{% include "partials/search-box.njk" %}
    {% set resultTools = { target: "[data-persona-grid]", noun: "personas", sort: true } %}{% include "partials/result-tools.njk" %}
  </div>


  <p data-persona-empty hidden role="status" aria-live="polite"><em>No persona matches that search.</em></p>
</section>

{# Faces a researcher or a vendor published with no identifier attached to any
   of them. They have no persona and cannot have one — there is nothing to
   attach a picture to but the post it came from — and they are kept because a
   published photograph of an operator's profile is a durable record of
   something the account itself will not keep. They sit at the end of the one
   grid, after everything that has an identity to be listed under, and their
   tiles link out to the publisher rather than inward to a page, which is the
   one place on this site a tile leaves it. #}
<section data-persona-section>
  <ul class="profile-grid" data-persona-grid>
    {% for persona in personas %}{% set cardPersona = persona %}{% include "partials/persona-card.njk" %}{% endfor %}
    {% for photo in loosePhotos %}
    {% set tile = {
      href: photo.post.url,
      photo: photo.file,
      name: photo.credit,
      sub: "Published " + photo.post.date,
      lang: "en",
      attrs: 'data-photograph data-search="' + (photo.credit | lower | escape) + ' photograph published without an identifier"'
    } %}
    {% include "partials/tile.njk" %}
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <p data-persona-more hidden>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" data-persona-more-button>Show the remaining personas</button>
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Disclaimer",
    preset: "not-proof",
    body: 'A persona name is the name an account presented under in the cited report, not necessarily the name of its operator.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}
</section>
